                {
                  "databaseId": 701,
                  "author": {
                    "login": "greptile-apps"
                  },
                  "body": "<a href=\"#\"><img alt=\"P1\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p1.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\"></a> **State file write is not atomic**\n\n`record()` reads, mutates and rewrites `state.json` with `write_text`. Two `/loop` passes recording at the same time can lose one update, and a crash mid-write leaves a truncated file that `load_state()` then silently treats as empty, so drafts and CI attempt counts are forgotten. Write to a temp file and `os.replace` it.",
                  "createdAt": "2026-10-29T09:00:00Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/rsvalerio/ai/pull/40#discussion_r701"
                }
              ]
            }
